# Commits that only moved whitespace and import lines around. Listing them here
# keeps `git blame` pointing at whoever wrote a line, not at whoever reformatted it.
#
# GitHub applies this file automatically. For local git:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Two rules, because git and GitHub both skip an unknown SHA in silence:
#
#   1. Add a commit here only if it changed no behaviour at all.
#   2. The SHA has to survive the merge. A squash or a rebase merge mints new
#      commits, so a pure-formatting commit must reach `main` either through a
#      merge commit or as its own squash, and the SHA recorded afterwards. CI
#      (the `history` job) fails if a listed SHA is not an ancestor of the
#      branch, so a squash that orphans one is loud rather than silent.

